# Performance Rules

## Measurement Discipline

- ALWAYS run `pnpm perf:benchmark` before claiming improvements
- ALWAYS compare against saved baseline with `pnpm perf:compare`
- Document actual numbers, not estimates
- Include test file sizes and durations in reports

## Main Thread Protection

- NEVER add synchronous CPU-intensive work to main thread
- ALL Whisper inference MUST run in Web Workers
- ALL FFmpeg processing MUST be non-blocking
- Use transferable objects for large data (Float32Array)

## Model Configuration

- Quantized models (`quantized: true`) are required for browser
- Distil models allowed if:
  - Accuracy impact measured and documented
  - User is informed (English-only warning)
  - Standard model remains available as option
- WebGPU optimizations MUST have WASM fallback

## Audio Enhancement Changes

- Default enhancements based on format:
  - MP4/WebM: disabled (usually pre-processed)
  - MKV/AVI/other: enabled (may need enhancement)
- User can always override defaults
- Time overhead must be displayed in UI

## Chunking Configuration

- Current: 30s chunks, 5s overlap (in worker)
- Changes require:
  - Accuracy testing at chunk boundaries
  - UX validation (no word splitting)
  - Performance measurement
